{8}$.\n\nFor $x < -2$, the polynomial is always positive.\n\nThe correct solution set is $(-\\infty, -2] \\cup [-1, \\frac{1-\\sqrt{33}}{8}] \\cup [\\frac{1+\\sqrt{33}}{8}, 2]$.\n\n```lean4\nimport Mathlib\n\nopen Real\n\n/-- The solution set of the inequality 4x⁴ + x² + 4x - 5x²|x+2| + 4 ≥ 0 -/\ntheorem solve_inequality_with_abs : \n  {x : ℝ | 4 * x^4 + x^2 + 4 * x - 5 * x^2 * abs (x + 2) + 4 ≥ 0} = \n  {x : ℝ | x ≤ -2 ∨ (-1 ≤ x ∧ x ≤ (1 - Real.sqrt 33) / 8) ∨ ((1 + Real.sqrt 33) / 8 ≤ x ∧ x ≤ 2)} := by sorry\n```<tool_call>\n{\"name\": \"leansearch\", \"arguments\": {\"query\": \"inequality absolute value solution set real numbers\", \"num_results\": 8}}\n</tool_call>\n<tool_response>\n[1] abs_le  (theorem)\n    ∀ {G : Type u_1} [inst : AddCommGroup G] [inst_1 : LinearOrder G] [IsOrderedAddMonoid G] {a b : G},\n  |a| ≤ b ↔ -b ≤ a ∧ a ≤ b\n    In an additive commutative group equipped with a linear order and compatible addition (i.e., an ordered additive commutative monoid), the absolute value of an element $a$ (defined as $\\sup(a, -a)$) satisfies $|a| \\leq b$ if and only if $-b \\leq a \\leq b$.\n[2] Set.mem_Icc_iff_abs_le  (theorem)\n    {R : Type*} [AddCommGroup R] [LinearOrder R] [IsOrderedAddMonoid R] {x y z : R} : |x - y| ≤ z ↔ y ∈ Icc (x - z) (x + z)\n    For elements $x, y, z$ in a linearly ordered additive commutative group with an ordered add monoid structure, the inequality $|\\,x - y\\,| \\leq z$ holds if and only if $y$ belongs to the closed interval $[x - z, x + z]$.\n[3] abs_sub_le_iff  (theorem)\n    ∀ {G : Type u_1} [inst : AddCommGroup G] [inst_1 : LinearOrder G] [IsOrderedAddMonoid G] {a b c : G},\n  |a - b| ≤ c ↔ a - b ≤ c ∧ b - a ≤ c\n    For any elements $a, b, c$ in an additive commutative group $G$ equipped with a linear order compatible with addition, the absolute value of $a - b$ is less than or equal to $c$ if and only if both $a - b \\leq c$ and $b - a \\leq c$.\n[4] abs_sub_lt_iff  (theorem)\n    ∀ {G : Type u_1} [inst : AddCommGroup 