roots of $ p $ is at most the number of distinct real roots of its derivative $ p' $ plus one. Symbolically, $ \\# \\text{roots}(p) \\leq \\# \\text{roots}(p') + 1 $.\n[2] Polynomial.card_roots_le_derivative  (theorem)\n    (p : ℝ[X]) : Multiset.card p.roots ≤ Multiset.card (derivative p).roots + 1\n    For any real polynomial $ p $, the cardinality of the multiset of roots of $ p $ is less than or equal to the cardinality of the multiset of roots of its formal derivative $ p' $ plus one, i.e., $ \\#\\text{roots}(p) \\leq \\#\\text{roots}(p') + 1 $.\n[3] Polynomial.card_rootSet_le_derivative  (theorem)\n    {F : Type*} [CommRing F] [Algebra F ℝ] (p : F[X]) :\n  Fintype.card (p.rootSet ℝ) ≤ Fintype.card (p.derivative.rootSet ℝ) + 1\n    For any polynomial $ p $ over a commutative ring $ F $ equipped with an $ \\mathbb{R} $-algebra structure, the cardinality of the set of distinct real roots of $ p $ is at most one greater than the cardinality of the set of distinct real roots of its derivative $ p' $. Formally, $ \\# \\text{Roots}(p) \\leq \\# \\text{Roots}(p') + 1 $.\n[4] Polynomial.quadratic_dvd_of_aeval_eq_zero_im_ne_zero  (theorem)\n    (p : ℝ[X]) {z : ℂ} (h0 : aeval z p = 0) (hz : z.im ≠ 0) : X ^ 2 - C (2 * z.re) * X + C (‖z‖ ^ 2) ∣ p\n    If a real polynomial $ p $ has a non-real complex root $ z $, then the quadratic polynomial $ X^2 - 2\\operatorname{Re}(z)X + \\|z\\|^2 $ divides $ p $, where $ \\|z\\|^2 = (\\operatorname{Re}(z))^2 + (\\operatorname{Im}(z))^2 $.\n[5] Polynomial.C_leadingCoeff_mul_prod_multiset_X_sub_C  (theorem)\n    (hroots : Multiset.card p.roots = p.natDegree) : C p.leadingCoeff * (p.roots.map fun a => X - C a).prod = p\n    If a nonzero polynomial $ p $ over an integral domain has exactly $ \\deg(p) $ roots (counting multiplicities), then $ p $ equals the product of its leading coefficient and the product of $ (X - a) $ for each root $ a $ in its root multiset, i.e., $ p = c \\prod_{a \\in \\text{roots}(p)} (X - a) $ where $ c $ is the leading coefficient.\n[6] Polynomial.roots_countP_pos_le_signVariations  (theorem)\n    : P.roots.countP (0 < ·) ≤ signVariations P\n    The number of positive real roots of a polynomial $ P $, counted with multiplicity, is less than or equal to the number of sign variations in its coefficients.\n[7] Polynomial.exists_prod_multiset_X_sub_C_mul  (theorem)\n    (p : R[X]) :\n  ∃ q, (p.roots.map fun a => X - C a).prod * q = p ∧ Multiset.card p.roots + q.natDegree = p.natDegree ∧ q.roots = 0\n    For any polynomial $ p $ over an integral domain $ R $, there exists a polynomial $ q $ such that $ p $ equals the product of $ (X - a) $ for each root $ a $ in the multiset of roots of $ p $ multiplied by $ q $. Additionally, the sum of the cardinality of the multiset of roots and the natural degree of $ q $ equals the natural degree of $ p $, and $ q $ has no roots.\n[8] Polynomial.mul_div_eq_iff_isRoot  (theorem)\n    : (X - C a) * (p / (X - C a)) = p ↔ IsRoot p a\n    For a polynomial $ p $ and an element $ a $, the equation $ (X - a) \\cdot \\left( \\frac{p}{X - a} \\right) = p $ holds if and only if $ a $ is a root of $ p $, i.e., $ p(a) = 0 $.\n</tool_response>\nNow I have enough information to formalize the correct solution. Let me verify the solution set by analyzing the inequality in two cases (x ≥ -2 and x < -2) and finding the correct intervals.\n\n```lean4\nimport Mathlib\n\nopen Real\n\n/-- The solution set of the inequality 4x⁴ + x² + 4x - 5x²|x+2| + 4 ≥ 0 -/\ntheorem solve_inequality_with_abs : \n  {x : ℝ | 4 * x^4 + x^2 + 4 * x - 5 * x^2 * abs (x + 2) + 4 ≥ 0} = \n  {x : ℝ | x ≤ -1 ∨ ((1 - Real.sqrt 33) / 8 ≤ x ∧ x ≤ (1 + Real.sqrt 33) / 8) ∨ x ≥ 2} := by sorry\n```\n\n# Round 2 (Semantic Self-validation)\n\nYour brief analysis:\n1. Math Assertion Analysis: The problem asks to solve the inequality $4 x^{4}+x^{2}+4 x-5 x^{2}|x+2|+4 \\geqslant 0$ for real $x$. This requires identifying the set of all real numbers $x$ that satisfy the condition.\n2. Lean Statement A